Haakon Studebaker wrote:

> How is it that I'm able to trigger a rolling boulder trap if I'm
> floating? I figure I'd be high above the tripwire or pressure plate.
> 
Physics.

Flying or levitation (which in real life probably means magnetic rather 
than magical) doesn't actually change the total downward force exerted by a 
body on the ground. I don't see why magic should have to break more 
physical laws than absolutely necessary. Magical levitation might well work 
by applying a downward force to lift you.


